**Problem**

What does the following conforming C program print? All arithmetic fits in int.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
static void change(int **p, int *q) {
    int *t = *p;
    *p = q;
    *t += **p;
    **p += 1;
}
int main(void) {
    int a[3] = {2,5,9};
    int *p = a;
    change(&p, a+1);
    change(&p, a);
    printf("%d %d %d\n", a[0], a[1], (int)(p-a));
    return 0;
}
```

**Candidate answers**
I. 7 13 0
II. 8 13 0
III. 8 6 1
IV. The program has undefined behaviour due to pointer aliasing.

